<http://data.silknow.org/object/3d22605b-3df4-3b90-89e7-231d0d7e0400>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Woman's petticoat of pale green silk taffeta lined with glazed undyed wool and wadded with a thin layer of wool.  It is quilted in running stitch with pale green silk thread in a border of geometric shapes with vertical flowers above, around the hem.  Above are 5 tiers of swags with very abstract flowers suspended. The petticoat is made of 7 panels of silk, with pocket openings in the side seams.  The hem is bound with ⅝-inch (1.6 cm) wide pale green silk ribbon.\n\nThe petticoat was altered in the late 19th century, probably for a studio prop. The original waist binding and ties were remove, the waist pleating reconfigured and stitched with linen tape."@en , "F, 1750-70, British; Pale green silk satin, quilted with flowers and swags, altered 1870-1910"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c333ea9f-8f76-3a2e-acac-71c91eba8e01> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "F, 1750-70, British; Pale green silk satin, quilted with flowers and swags, altered 1870-1910"@en , "Woman's petticoat of pale green silk taffeta lined with glazed undyed wool and wadded with a thin layer of wool.  It is quilted in running stitch with pale green silk thread in a border of geometric shapes with vertical flowers above, around the hem.  Above are 5 tiers of swags with very abstract flowers suspended. The petticoat is made of 7 panels of silk, with pocket openings in the side seams.  The hem is bound with ⅝-inch (1.6 cm) wide pale green silk ribbon.\n\nThe petticoat was altered in the late 19th century, probably for a studio prop. The original waist binding and ties were remove, the waist pleating reconfigured and stitched with linen tape."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/3d22605b-3df4-3b90-89e7-231d0d7e0400/dimension/3> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/3d22605b-3df4-3b90-89e7-231d0d7e0400/dimension/4> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/3d22605b-3df4-3b90-89e7-231d0d7e0400/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/3d22605b-3df4-3b90-89e7-231d0d7e0400/dimension/1> ;
